  triage:title "docs/atm-core/boundaries.md and backing TOMLs still describe SourceIngress/ProjectionExport as live contracts" ;
  triage:description "AI1-QA-1 (2026-07-20) on PR #592 found docs/atm-core/boundaries.md:285-348 still documents SourceIngress/ProjectionExport as live contracts (present-tense prose plus forward-looking 'Phase Yb'/'Phase Yc' language) despite zero implementing code anywhere in crates/ after the AI.1 cross-host/peer-transport deletion (confirmed: no `impl SourceIngress`/`impl ProjectionExport` anywhere in crates/). Backing TOMLs boundaries/atm-core/inbox-ingress.toml and boundaries/atm-core/inbox-export.toml still declare state='stub_landed'/'concrete_landed' instead of 'retired'. inbox-export.toml's named_callers list (`atm_core::direct_boundaries::export_source_files`, `atm_core::direct_boundaries::reexport_messages`) reference functions confirmed absent from crates/atm-core/src/direct_boundaries.rs (grep returns zero matches for either function name; the file exists but the functions do not). Same defect class as ARCH-003/RBQA-F008 (already fixed on the atm-daemon side), left unaddressed on the atm-core side." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
